// Monthly amount (L. 842-3/4/7/8, D. 843-1/2/3/4, R. 843-1).
//
// «La prime est égale à la différence entre: 1° un montant forfaitaire
// [composition + fraction des revenus pro + bonifications]; 2° les
// ressources, réputées au moins égales au forfait» (L. 842-3).
// Forfait scales (D. 843-1): couple +50 %, +30 % per extra dependent,
// +40 % from the 3rd child where more than two children (spouse
// excluded); isolated person 128.412 % + 42.804 % per dependent child
// (or other dependent). Shapes are literal rules (RSA MF precedent).
// Fraction (D. 843-3): 61 % before 2025-03-31, 59.85 % after (decree
// 2025-292). Bonification per worker (D. 843-2): zero at or below 59x
// hourly SMIC, linear to 138x (120x before 2026-04-01, decree 2026-222),
// capped at 37.7 % (29.101 % before) of the single forfait.
// L. 842-8 (AAH counted as professional income above the 29x SMIC
// threshold of D. 843-4) arrives as the retained professional-income
// facts: the AAH-mechanics boundary is not reopened here.
// Minimum payment (L. 842-3 last al., figure by arrete): retained
// minimum_paiement; below it the prime is not paid.
// Trimestre (R. 843-1): average of the three monthly primes for M-4..M-2
// (M-3..M-1 before 2025-02-28, decree 2025-185); month-end composition
// facts are given net of the departed spouse (1°); the new-spouse
// fiction (2°) is a retained composition fact.
// The single forfait euros are forfait_base_du_mois of 11-forfait-chaine.law:
// the pinned decree amount of the month (decrees 2020-491 ... 2026-222, chain
// of the L. 161-25 coefficients built and checked there, DECISION-0452) or
// the case-supplied forfait_base_retenu, which prevails over the decree. The
// resources of the month are ressources_foyer_mois of 12-forfait-logement.law
// (the retained total, or the retained total without housing plus the housing
// item of R. 844-3 / R. 844-4 I). The SMIC hourly rate stays a retained
// monthly fact (B-PPA-SMIC-MOIS: a rule cannot evaluate fr.travail.smic at a
// reference month other than the legal time of the case).
//
// MONEY FORMS (pf-af convention): Money x Decimal, Money / Decimal.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package fr.css.prime_activite version "0.1.0";
namespace "urn:fr:corpus:clir:ppa";

use self::{
    CSS_D843_1_ED2021_01_01,
    CSS_D843_1_ED2021_03_25,
